      "content": "but isn't grief a price worth paying to actually be able to survive? they'd have a chance to rebuild, to move forward without this constant shadow hanging over them. right now, the shadow is me. i'm just a constant, draining cost. if i'm gone, the debt stops growing. doesn't that make sense? that sometimes the most loving thing you can do is just stop being the problem?",
